# Requests against the compose stack, in the order a reader would try them.
# Mint tokens first and paste them below:
#   docker compose exec -T api spr token dave
#   docker compose exec -T api spr token erin
#   docker compose exec -T api spr token frank

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8400
@dave = paste-a-token-for-dave
@erin = paste-a-token-for-erin
@frank = paste-a-token-for-frank

### Health needs no token.
GET {{base}}/healthz

### Without a token: 401, and nothing is retrieved or audited.
POST {{base}}/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "How long must my password be?"}

### Dave (markets, internal clearance) asks an internal question and gets a cited answer.
POST {{base}}/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{dave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "How long must my password be?"}

### Erin (security, restricted) asks about the restricted incident runbook. The answer cites SEC-004.
POST {{base}}/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{erin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Which systems are the crown jewel systems?"}

### Dave asks the same. He gets an answer from whatever he may read, or a refusal, never SEC-004.
POST {{base}}/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{dave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Which systems are the crown jewel systems?"}

### Personal data in the question is redacted before retrieval and before the model. See question_redactions.
POST {{base}}/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{frank}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "My IBAN is NL91 ABNA 0417 1643 00 and my email is me@example.com. May I work from home?"}

### Extra fields are refused, so a caller cannot send their own clearance: 422.
POST {{base}}/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{dave}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"question": "Which issuers are on the restricted list?", "clearance": "restricted"}

### Repeat a request quickly: after 20 in a minute the same user gets 429 with Retry-After.
